{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview","id":1121324,"title":"Contracts of Steed [Second Edition Preview]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-27T08:37:00-07:00","id":1121324,"title":"Contracts of Steed [Second Edition Preview]","content":"See it below. Looks interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\"> Contracts of Steed [Changeling: The Lost] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/contracts-of-steed-changeling-the-lost/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T09:48:48-07:00","id":1121350,"title":"","content":"Bearing in mind it's obviously past the time to change anything and I'm just exposing the impression and feelings this preview gives me.<br /> <br /> It's a curious division and it seems to make arcadian contracts more uniform in terms of purchasing and acquiring them, but I'm not sure the in-universe distinction between Common and Royal contracts (or their origins, rather) serves that significant a purpose.<br /> <br /> There only being two levels of potency also looks more restrictive than helpful bearing in mind the myriad of contracts within a wide band of power that have previously existed. I'm reflexively concerned it's going to lead to some flattening of the potential of contracts, or more pertinently, significant skews in usefulness between contracts that are categorized as roughly the same level. There seems to be some of that in the preview, which makes me a bit skeptical.<br /> <br /> Though, I'm making some potentially very wrong assumptions. I could be misinterpreting what the categorization means in practice, but if it's based on their origin and not necessarily their level of power then I still worry about inequalities in the value of contracts, and if it doesn't directly tie to contract costs I'm left wondering why make it so, and what information we're missing here because it seems pertinent. Some clarification would be really appreciated.<br /> <br /> Also, Chrysalis seems like the exact definition of a Mirror contract. I'm confused why it's in Steed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Having seen Rose clarify the Experiences costs for the contracts, alright, that's not far from what I expected. Several of my doubts remain, particularly about the discrepancy of value between contracts and the flattening of their pricing, and I'm not sure how to feel about the conclusions reached in the redesign, hmm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-27-2017, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:15:43-07:00","id":1121366,"title":"","content":"In designing new Contracts, you use the power level to determine the origin. If it works with existing resources, the Others would have willingly let their servants have it. If it's more overtly creative (or so transformative as to essentially be creative), it's the kind of thing they would have kept to themselves.<br /> <br /> (There are exceptions, of course, where Keepers might have added changelings as beneficiaries of Royal Contracts.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: The behind-the-scenes reasoning is that we did initial drafts and playtests with a full five dot range of Contracts. That ended up feeling like too much granularity: the powers we found were most fun for changelings didn't break down naturally into five power brackets, with distinctions between, for example, 4 and 5 dots feeling really fuzzy. So then we thought &quot;why would Contracts vary in power in the first place?&quot; and that led to breaking away from the old WW structure and more towards DtD's categorization of &quot;moderate power&quot; and &quot;major power.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've found it works pretty well, and it took a lot of guesswork and arbitrary decisions out of building additional Contracts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-27-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:28:05-07:00","id":1121373,"title":"","content":"(By the way, if anyone's interested in hearing the reasoning behind why VtR2's powers stuck to five dot ladders, I'd be happy to talk about it, and it might shed some light on why that's not as good a fit for CtL. But I'd rather not just go off on a tangent about a different game in the <i>Changeling</i> forum.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:30:02-07:00","id":1121375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121373#post1121373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(By the way, if anyone's interested in hearing the reasoning behind why VtR2's powers stuck to five dot ladders, I'd be happy to talk about it, and it might shed some light on why that's not as good a fit for CtL. But I'd rather not just go off on a tangent about a different game in the <i>Changeling</i> forum.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I for one would be very interested to hear the reasoning. Game mechanics and background lore are as fascinating as game play itself for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:43:17-07:00","id":1121384,"title":"","content":"Ach, no! My Hedge Sorcerers! They're going to need a rewrite...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121373#post1121373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(By the way, if anyone's interested in hearing the reasoning behind why VtR2's powers stuck to five dot ladders, I'd be happy to talk about it, and it might shed some light on why that's not as good a fit for CtL. But I'd rather not just go off on a tangent about a different game in the <i>Changeling</i> forum.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:48:27-07:00","id":1121387,"title":"","content":"Aside from Court Contracts (if they exist) that's pretty much all the details of new Contract system into place. Looks like Contracts end up on the cheaper side but not as big a gulf from other Supernatural Templates as it was in 1st ed. I think Minor-Medium-Major would be better fit some of the previous contract dynamics, but upgrading anything that would be a minor to medium seems fine too.<br /> <br /> Is there like a Merit or something to let people pick up new animal forms for Chrysalis?<br /> <br /> Talon and Wing possibly granting aggravated damage is pretty potent, particularly if things like Fighting Styles count as to whether or not your unarmed strikes do lethal.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T10:51:22-07:00","id":1121390,"title":"","content":"Thank you for taking the time to explain, Rose. Putting it like that it's certainly easier to understand the reasoning despite my misgivings. The appeal of diminishing granularity is simple to see and is a logical conclusion, but I feel like it risks exchanging fiddly mechanical specification for a more ambiguous distinction and potential power discrepancies? Just as an example, I would not have pegged Talon and Wing as a Royal Contract based on its breadth or depth of use, and I wouldn't call it the same level of effect* as the other Royal contracts.<br /> <br /> I assume that sort of thing was noted, but ultimately the conveniences of this model outweighted the design concerns?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Granted, I also wouldn't give access to Aggravated damage to a &quot;Minor&quot; power, even if it's contigent on character creation choices that a majority of Changelings won't make. A Minor-Medium-Major division like what schizoPOP suggested above would've been a more balanced scheme to me.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">It is a more elegant solution however, and I'm satisfied to hear the reasons behind it.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-27-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:10:28-07:00","id":1121408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121375#post1121375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one would be very interested to hear the reasoning. Game mechanics and background lore are as fascinating as game play itself for me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, when I first got asked to pitch a new edition of <i>Vampire</i>, one of the things I knew I wanted to emphasize was <i>becoming</i> a vampire. In first edition, we had written some setting stuff as if vampirism was a slow slide from light into darkness, and other stuff as if the Embrace was like flipping a light switch. Based on a lot of experience running the game and having talked to lots of other players over the years, I felt that the former was more narratively compelling.<br /> <br /> The obvious mechanical scales of transition in becoming a vampire are Humanity and Blood Potency, but I thought there was the potential to show powers themselves as forms of evolution away from human life. And they're forms of evolution that the player has a lot of input into, so the &quot;you did this&quot; theme of <i>Vampire</i> gets heavily emphasized.<br /> <br /> I also felt that every vampire power should be scary and predatory -- the tag line for that was &quot;horror from dot one,&quot; and it was the first guiding principle. The second guiding principle was that if a player buys even one dot of a power, they should be able to do the thing that power's known for. So, for example, one dot of Majesty lets you impress people even when your hands are covered in blood, one dot of Obfuscate lets you go unnoticed, and one dot of Auspex lets you dig out secrets.<br /> <br /> So the dev team came up with what I called a telescoping structure for the dot ladder. Dot one is a broadly useful power that summarizes the concept of the Discipline. Dot two builds on dot one, and sometimes introduces an element of risk. Dot three and dot four are bigger boosts that expand the breadth of the power. Each of these steps so far is a form of growing toward monstrosity -- the more you have these powers, the more you'll use them to solve your problems, the more you'll need to drink the blood of the living. And then dot five... well, dot five is a bit of a big step up. It's the one that tells you you're really not bound my the definition of &quot;human&quot; anymore. It makes you impossibly beloved or gives you a form that's not even a body. Using it is bound to change your perspective.<br /> <br /> The particular set of Disciplines was retained from 1e because they covered things that everybody who's read vampire books or watched vampire movies know that vampires can do. Vampires are, in many way, our most traditionally archetypal monsters.<br /> <br /> This is a solid way of designing a power structure, but it's very particular to the themes of <i>Vampire</i> and the way we felt individual Requiems might develop.<br /> <br /> But not every monster in the World of Darkness is like that. And for all that Lost have in common with Kindred, that's almost the opposite of <i>Changeling</i>'s arc. The stories of the Lost are about building and reclaiming lives that were taken away. They start pretty supernaturally potent as a result of the ways they were changed in Arcadia and the ways they fought for their freedom. For a changeling, powers represent parlaying the difficult hand you're dealt into the tools you need to get the life you want.<br /> <br /> So rather than a self-reinforcing ladder of horror, gaining power as a changeling is about snatching advantages where you can, turning the rules and laws of your Keeper and their kind against them, using every trick you've got to make it in the world. Goblin Contracts are a thing for a reason -- sometimes you've just got to cut a deal with a downside.<br /> <br /> Changeling powers don't represent <i>evolution</i>, they represent <i>opportunities</i>. And so instead of dribbling out power a little at a time in narrow channels that make you into something else, we present bigger powers that ask for trickier, slipperier, more fairy tale use.<br /> <br /> The next question becomes &quot;where do those powers come from?&quot; And the answer for Arcadian Contracts is that they come from deals made by the rightfully-despised Gentry.* A changeling taking a power isn't becoming less human and more fae -- they're snatching an advantage and using it to become more <i>themselves</i>, or at least to protect that life and identity.<br /> <br /> Combine that with the design/testing experience we had, what we've learned from the half-dozen other lines we've played with power structures for, and the desire to make it easy for players to make new powers, and you get what we have here: power categories with bright-line divisions that represent risks taken, opportunities snatched, power claimed from the very things that sought to box you in.<br /> <br /> <br /> (* Court Contracts come from a somewhat different place, which will be described in the book. Guidelines for making new Contracts of various kinds are in Chapter 7.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-27-2017, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T11:32:28-07:00","id":1121424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121384#post1121384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ach, no! My Hedge Sorcerers! They're going to need a rewrite...</div> </div> </div> </div>You might find the Hedgespinning rules useful for that, depending on where you're coming from with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:04:25-07:00","id":1121442,"title":"","content":"Is it still true that your available Contracts effect your Mien?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:20:00-07:00","id":1121452,"title":"","content":"I'm really liking that there is a specific place in the Hedge called the &quot;Mirror Realm&quot; where all mirrors either do or have the opportunity to connect to. That is a change that I really really like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T12:32:08-07:00","id":1121458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121442#post1121442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it still true that your available Contracts effect your Mien?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's from Chapter 3: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 3, Contracts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once a changeling signs onto a Contract, it changes her forever. A Contract isn't just something the changeling uses; it's a bond she\u2019s made through the Wyrd. Entering a Contract with smoke makes the world seem a little bit darker, while entering a Contract with stone gives her skin a mottled gray appearance. When the changeling invokes a Contract, she can perceive the power it was bargained from, be it as whispers in flames, faces in stone, or another effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:06:25-07:00","id":1121478,"title":"","content":"Before Changelings got 5 dots of contracts to start out with, but how many contracts (Royal and Common) does the Changeling get to start off with at Character creation? <br /> <br /> Also if Royal Contracts are deals the True Fae made that Changelings sign onto and Court Contracts are deals the Courts made, them what are Royal Court Contracts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:12:29-07:00","id":1121479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121478#post1121478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before Changelings got 5 dots of contracts to start out with, but how many contracts (Royal and Common) does the Changeling get to start off with at Character creation?</div> </div> </div> </div> Your character begins with four Contracts chosen from among Common Regalia, Common Court, and Goblin Contracts; she must meet the proper requirements to take Court Contracts. Two of those starting Contracts must come from the character\u2019s favored Regalia. She also gains two Royal Contracts from her Court or favored Regalia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121478#post1121478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if Royal Contracts are deals the True Fae made that Changelings sign onto and Court Contracts are deals the Courts made, them what are Royal Court Contracts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Court Contracts also come in Common and Royal categories. In this case \u201croyalty,\u201d rather than being those who rise to the levels of the Others, are those who rise to the levels of the Court founders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T13:17:29-07:00","id":1121483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121479#post1121479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Your character begins with four Contracts chosen from among Common Regalia, Common Court, and Goblin Contracts; she must meet the proper requirements to take Court Contracts. Two of those starting Contracts must come from the character\u2019s favored Regalia. She also gains two Royal Contracts from her Court or favored Regalia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Court Contracts also come in Common and Royal categories. In this case \u201croyalty,\u201d rather than being those who rise to the levels of the Others, are those who rise to the levels of the Court founders.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks, so a character starts off with 4 common or Goblin Contracts and 2 Royal Contracts from her Court or Favoured Regalia. Cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T14:38:57-07:00","id":1121552,"title":"","content":"So far example you could make a starting Beast with Dreamsteps, Pathfinder, Boon of the Scuttling Spider, Seven League Leap, Chrystalist, and Mirror Walk for example is pretty, powerful, although it's still on par roughly with what the other splats can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:23:28-07:00","id":1121571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121424#post1121424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You might find the Hedgespinning rules useful for that, depending on where you're coming from with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\">Hedge Sorcerers</a> were basically Mortal + Contracts (gotten via bargain with Goblins, Fae, the Wyrd itself, or whatever). They basically just bought them as merits, and took advantage of the Catch to activate them since they didn't have Glamour.<br /> <br /> They actually weren't connected to the Hedge (necessarily) - it was more of a play on words with Hedge Mage (low magic users) and Hedge being associate with Changeling. I'm not sure if Hedgeshaping will fill that niche? I could probably keep it more or less the same, maybe limiting it to the Common Contracts or something. Loophole still allows for Glamour-less activation, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:30:45-07:00","id":1121581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121571#post1121571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/952550-minor-micro-template-hedge-sorcerers\">Hedge Sorcerers</a> were basically Mortal + Contracts (gotten via bargain with Goblins, Fae, the Wyrd itself, or whatever). They basically just bought them as merits, and took advantage of the Catch to activate them since they didn't have Glamour.<br /> <br /> They actually weren't connected to the Hedge (necessarily) - it was more of a play on words with Hedge Mage (low magic users) and Hedge being associate with Changeling. I'm not sure if Hedgeshaping will fill that niche? I could probably keep it more or less the same, maybe limiting it to the Common Contracts or something. Loophole still allows for Glamour-less activation, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Yes, loophole is just the new name for first edition's Catch, so your sorcerers could totally use Common Contracts and fulfill their loopholes. You could also consider letting them invoke Common Contracts as if they were Goblin Contracts, building up goblin debt and so on.<br /> <br /> Hedgespinning (shaping the Hedge to a changeling's desires or feelings) is the main form of Hedge-based magic we have in the core book, but I've got ideas for some other kinds of Hedge-dependent magic. We'll see where the KS stretch goals and the supplements go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T18:21:36-07:00","id":1121647,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm stoked. From the looks of it, I can get to designing Ziggy's Grace of the Moon Beast contract as a Royal Steed contract. It might be simpler to combine and reskin some of these, though.<br /> <br /> Basic idea: He can manipulate his personal gravity, immunity to fall damage and falling objects.<br /> <br /> Boon of the Scuttling Spider is good for walking on walls.<br /> Seven Leagues Leap is good for gravity-assisted jumping and running &quot;downhill&quot; in a chase, as well as giving him a mean dropkick if he picks up the Ogre effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T19:40:56-07:00","id":1121672,"title":"","content":"This looks rather nice and more consistent than 1e style contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T21:43:36-07:00","id":1121708,"title":"","content":"So what dinosaurs might be within the range of an Ogre?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T22:00:25-07:00","id":1121713,"title":"","content":"If you're talking about size then as big as an elephant, so that looks like T. Rex or Triceratops or something smaller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 07-28-2017, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T00:41:17-07:00","id":1121745,"title":"","content":"The Common/Royal division in Contracts makes me think of how fairy tales often had different endings depending on whether the audience was a peasant or an aristocrat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T03:28:36-07:00","id":1121766,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> Any instructions or guidelines on how to convert 1ed Contracts to 2ed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:14:14-07:00","id":1121894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121766#post1121766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2\" data-vbnamecard=\"2\">Rose Bailey</a> Any instructions or guidelines on how to convert 1ed Contracts to 2ed?</div> </div> </div> </div>The guidelines for creating Contracts in Chapter 7 should cover this. You'd take a clause out of a 1e Contract, decide whether it's Common or Royal (which is more about the type of effect than the dot level), and pick a Regalia. Then you'd add seeming clauses... for a comprehensive conversion, you'd want to do two, but if you just want to update the power for your character, just make one extra benefit for whatever their seeming is.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The other thing is that not every 1e Contract is going to be five 2e Contracts. Some of those dot levels can be merged together. And a few might even be better fits as changeling-specific Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 07-28-2017, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T09:16:57-07:00","id":1121898,"title":"","content":"I like all the new and innovative changes to powers second edition is doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T11:54:11-07:00","id":1121982,"title":"","content":"I'm loving this write-up something fierce, won't lie. My hype for 2e Ling has been growing more and more with the recent previews, and I can't wait for the book to come out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Pay no attention to the man behind the Storyteller!&quot; <hr /><a href=\"https://www.fromdusktilljawn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">From Dusk 'til Jawn</a> - 2e nWoD game set in Philadelphia<br /> <a href=\"http://www.gravenlore.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Graven Lore</a> - 2e multi-venue nWoD game<br /> <a href=\"http://newhaven.mindrealms.com/\" target=\"_blank\">New Haven</a> - 2e nWoD game set in southern Maine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/951-caelene","name":"Caelene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T19:43:27-07:00","id":1122170,"title":"","content":"Something i didnt quite understood about this new contracts. It seems that the only difference between common and royal contracts is power level (the royals being normally more powerful) on the mechanical side, is that true?<br /> <br /> Will there be any extra cost besides XP for getting contracts, royal or common? Or its the 1E method of &quot;you do communion with the chosen aspect and deal but said deal doesnt have a mechanical backing&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T06:41:59-07:00","id":1122319,"title":"","content":"I love the fact that more CoD lines are moving away from the 5 dot powers to other constructs that fit them better. This worked great for both Werewolf and Beast and I believe it will for Changelings too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T06:53:16-07:00","id":1122324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1122319#post1122319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love the fact that more CoD lines are moving away from the 5 dot powers to other constructs that fit them better. This worked great for both Werewolf and Beast and I believe it will for Changelings too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy did it too (first?) with Affinities and Utterances.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T07:56:00-07:00","id":1122337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1122324#post1122324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy did it too (first?) with Affinities and Utterances.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So did Demon with Embeds and Exploits, as was mentioned by Rose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/24296274/BeastThePrimordial.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6566-draca","name":"Draca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6566_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T14:02:40-07:00","id":1122470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1121581#post1121581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I see. Yes, loophole is just the new name for first edition's Catch, so your sorcerers could totally use Common Contracts and fulfill their loopholes. You could also consider letting them invoke Common Contracts as if they were Goblin Contracts, building up goblin debt and so on.<br /> <br /> Hedgespinning (shaping the Hedge to a changeling's desires or feelings) is the main form of Hedge-based magic we have in the core book, but I've got ideas for some other kinds of Hedge-dependent magic. We'll see where the KS stretch goals and the supplements go.</div> </div> </div> </div> That sounds interesting, looking forward to that KS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T14:15:45-07:00","id":1122477,"title":"","content":"I had assumed that Steed was Beast (I was right,, easy one), Sword is Ogre, Crown Fairest, Shield Wizened, Mirror Darkling, and Jewel Elemental. <br /> <br /> But having read what each of these Regalia focus on, Jewel is manipulation and temptation which would suggest Darkling (I have to remember not all Jewels are bright, some are dark, like Onyx).<br /> <br /> Mirror is perception and self transformation and Shield is protection. I could see either being, Elemental or, Wizened, that's hard to place. <br /> <br /> Phantom Glory will likely be Mirror, but protection from elementals will likely be Shield. Still I'm leaning towards Mirror being Elementals Regalia, and Shield being Wizened. It could be the reverse still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T19:36:37-07:00","id":1122572,"title":"","content":"If the concepts remained the same, it should be Elemental, Wizened, and Darkling for Shield, Mirror, and Jewel; survivalist, skilled, sneak. No idea about what it will actually be though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T00:58:32-07:00","id":1122646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1122572#post1122572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the concepts remained the same, it should be Elemental, Wizened, and Darkling for Shield, Mirror, and Jewel; survivalist, skilled, sneak. No idea about what it will actually be though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Could be, you make a good arguement for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T10:15:41-07:00","id":1122735,"title":"","content":"I like this. A bit more structure than the former previews, which I feel will help in creating characters. Looking forward to the KS <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T16:10:46-07:00","id":1152054,"title":"","content":"Something that kind of bothers me about Chrysalis is how the two Seeming benefits interact with Beasts. If any other Seeming gets Chrysalis, they can pick up the Beast portion later to gain access to two other animals. However, a Beast naturally gets that benefit as soon as they purchase the contract, which means that unless they purchase the Ogre benefit as soon as they get the contract, they can't choose any animals over size 15 and the Ogre benefit becomes redundant to gain because, well, you can't get any more animal forms. A Beast with Chrysalis at character creation outright can't get them at all because, as far as I know, there is no option for buying Out-of-Seeming contract benefits that early.<br /> <br /> The wording is a bit problematic for a Beast is what I'm getting at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T19:31:19-07:00","id":1152091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1152054#post1152054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that kind of bothers me about Chrysalis is how the two Seeming benefits interact with Beasts. If any other Seeming gets Chrysalis, they can pick up the Beast portion later to gain access to two other animals. However, a Beast naturally gets that benefit as soon as they purchase the contract, which means that unless they purchase the Ogre benefit as soon as they get the contract, they can't choose any animals over size 15 and the Ogre benefit becomes redundant to gain because, well, you can't get any more animal forms. A Beast with Chrysalis at character creation outright can't get them at all because, as far as I know, there is no option for buying Out-of-Seeming contract benefits that early.<br /> <br /> The wording is a bit problematic for a Beast is what I'm getting at.</div> </div> </div> </div> Did not notice that, I'd personally allow the person to trade out two current forms for 2 size 15 forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-22T20:27:49-07:00","id":1152098,"title":"","content":"Erg, misremembered what the Ogre bonus gave - it allows <i>up to</i> size 15 forms, not above that. It's still problematic though, because the contract still requires those forms when the contract is purchased, and without the Ogre bonus the forms are limited to size 7.<br /> <br /> My solution would be to instead make it so a Changeling can add those forms as she chooses, rather than immediately when getting the seeming bonus. Admittedly there aren't a lot of animals above size 7 a Changeling would want to casually change into, but it's still something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T08:07:35-07:00","id":1152510,"title":"","content":"I don't particularly see a problem, to be honest. If you're a Beast that's going to be investing in Chrysalis, you generally have your forms in mind already. Lets say that you're playing a spider themed beast. When you take Chrysalis, you'll be picking a small spider the size of a palm, a large spider, a drider/arachne form, and... something else spidery. You'll be picking the stats that work for the form you're picking. If the Beast was something dragon-themed and wanted to use elephant stats to represent that, then they'd be getting Ogre right away.<br /> <br /> Experience has shown that most players will be picking their forms at the time of purchase, or as early as character creation, and then rarely varying from those initial forms. This even holds true for things like Protean magic - people pick certain themes and generally stick with them. <br /> <br /> This is one of those situations that seem theoretically possible, but haven't really seen it come up in actual play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T08:18:58-07:00","id":1152512,"title":"","content":"I must admit I'm still confused why Chrysalis was included in the Contracts of Steed in the preview, when it seems like the very definition of a Contract of Mirror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T09:03:40-07:00","id":1152528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1152510#post1152510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't particularly see a problem, to be honest. If you're a Beast that's going to be investing in Chrysalis, you generally have your forms in mind already. Lets say that you're playing a spider themed beast. When you take Chrysalis, you'll be picking a small spider the size of a palm, a large spider, a drider/arachne form, and... something else spidery. You'll be picking the stats that work for the form you're picking. If the Beast was something dragon-themed and wanted to use elephant stats to represent that, then they'd be getting Ogre right away.<br /> <br /> Experience has shown that most players will be picking their forms at the time of purchase, or as early as character creation, and then rarely varying from those initial forms. This even holds true for things like Protean magic - people pick certain themes and generally stick with them. <br /> <br /> This is one of those situations that seem theoretically possible, but haven't really seen it come up in actual play.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that if you are a Beast starting with Chrysalis, you can\u2019t buy the Ogre seeming bonus, as there is no option for that. You are stuck with buying four forms, all between size one and seven. That is fine for a spider themed Beast, but what about an aquatic one? No sharks or whales that are much larger than a person. No elephants, rhinos, rocs or even large dragons and dinosaurs.<br /> <br /> Granted, size seven-through-fifteen animals aren\u2019t entirely practical, but my point is that a Beast is effectively locked out of the option unless they immediately spend another experience. What point is there of getting the Ogre benefit if you can\u2019t use it, since the Beast option is immediately in effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-24-2017, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T11:01:37-07:00","id":1152558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1152528#post1152528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that if you are a Beast starting with Chrysalis, you can\u2019t buy the Ogre seeming bonus, as there is no option for that. You are stuck with buying four forms, all between size one and seven. That is fine for a spider themed Beast, but what about an aquatic one? No sharks or whales that are much larger than a person. No elephants, rhinos, rocs or even large dragons and dinosaurs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or have a baby whale that grows up to full size when you get the Ogre clause a session and half later. Or the ST says to just leave a slot open to be decided upon later. Or just seal the form until the Ogre clause is purchased. Or be a Beast that has affinity for both the Beast and Ogre Regalia; you start with two, as I recall, so you should be able to have a PC with both Ogre and Beast clauses for free. Or start off as an ogre and get Chrysalis and not the Beast clause. Or just get another Royal Contract and buy Chrysalis later when you have the XP; there's a lot of very good Royal Contracts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Granted, size seven-through-fifteen animals aren\u2019t entirely practical, but my point is that a Beast is effectively locked out of the option unless they immediately spend another experience. What point is there of getting the Ogre benefit if you can\u2019t use it, since the Beast option is immediately in effect? </div> </div> </div> Its only locked out in a very niche situation that's very unlikely to show up in play. Theorycrafting a problem is nice and all, but I have to question if such a problem will ever show up in game play. You have to be a Beast that wants to be an impractically large creature but refuses to take the Ogre regalia and insists on taking Chrysalis as a starting Contract, with no flexibility at all on anyone's end. A situation you need a conversion of several notable details all line up all at once. <br /> <br /> Is this something that's actually happening, or is it something we only see in a white room?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T11:26:09-07:00","id":1152568,"title":"","content":"And, y\u2019know, we don\u2019t really know the details on if one can purchase all the Seeming clauses. <br /> <br /> Unless if there was a preview for Rose\u2019s/Meghan\u2019s CtL2 that I missed that says otherwise...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T16:01:27-07:00","id":1152626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1121324-contracts-of-steed-second-edition-preview?p=1152558#post1152558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or have a baby whale that grows up to full size when you get the Ogre clause a session and half later. Or the ST says to just leave a slot open to be decided upon later. Or just seal the form until the Ogre clause is purchased. Or be a Beast that has affinity for both the Beast and Ogre Regalia; you start with two, as I recall, so you should be able to have a PC with both Ogre and Beast clauses for free. Or start off as an ogre and get Chrysalis and not the Beast clause. Or just get another Royal Contract and buy Chrysalis later when you have the XP; there's a lot of very good Royal Contracts.<br /> <br /> Its only locked out in a very niche situation that's very unlikely to show up in play. Theorycrafting a problem is nice and all, but I have to question if such a problem will ever show up in game play. You have to be a Beast that wants to be an impractically large creature but refuses to take the Ogre regalia and insists on taking Chrysalis as a starting Contract, with no flexibility at all on anyone's end. A situation you need a conversion of several notable details all line up all at once.<br /> <br /> Is this something that's actually happening, or is it something we only see in a white room?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Happening to any Beast who buys Chrysalis&quot; is hardly a niche situation, especially since Royal contracts are not cheap. Effectively adding another experience on top of that removes the benefit of it being synergetic with Beasts in the first place, since a Favored Regalia is only cheaper by 1 experience.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I haven't read anything that allows you to get the Ogre seeming bonuses alongside the Beast's seeming bonuses - having a Favored Regalia simply means you pay less than for a contract that isn't in your Favored Regalia. Beasts get a Favored Regalia in Steed, but getting a Favored Regalia in Mirror won't give you seeming bonuses for the seeming that would normally have Mirror as a Favored Regalia; they are not &quot;Beast Regalia&quot; or &quot;Ogre Regalia&quot;, and getting an Ogre's Favored Regalia does not make the Changeling part Ogre. Any contracts in Mirrors will simply be cheaper, and the only seeming bonuses you'd get for free are ones belonging to Beasts. Even if it did work that way, it'd be a pretty big band-aid for fixing a single contract given it permanently decides a part of the character. This goes even more so if the player outright starts as an Ogre to avoid the problem.<br /> <br /> As for the modded solutions, that is what I was saying earlier - as written, another seeming has more functionality from Chrysalis than a Beast would, and so it needs to be modded. One solution you proposed is exactly the same as one I suggested earlier, allowing one with the Beast seeming bonus to take new forms at a later time, rather than as soon as the seeming bonus is acquired.<br /> <br /> I do admit, though, taking a baby-whale form and then making it an adult with the Ogre seeming bonus is pretty novel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 10-24-2017, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}